### Research targets

1. Faithfully compare published KM moves
   with our native semantics. For a declared
   substantive operation family, prove an
   effective simulation with explicit costs,
   or a kernel-checked obstruction to that
   comparison. Distinguish algebraic
   identities from legal state transitions.

2. Use that comparison to justify one
   reusable contextual extension beyond
   the five-circuit catalogue. Establish
   effective paths, family coverage,
   restoration, carrier invariants, and
   expanded length/altitude bounds—or refute
   the predeclared substantive contract.

Predeclare scope; do not shrink it after
failed examples. Never silently change
states, coefficients, moves, or competitors.
Novelty requires comparison with prior art,
not formalization or unsuccessful retrieval.
Recommend a pivot if faithful comparison
leaves no meaningful strengthening; do not
substitute more enumeration.

